WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.875
Before the code, the model.

2
00:00:01.875 --> 00:00:04.263
Learn describes two kinds of policy.

3
00:00:04.263 --> 00:00:08.269
There's one tenant default, which
always exists and starts switched off,

4
00:00:08.269 --> 00:00:10.985
with separate restrictions
for apps that live in

5
00:00:10.985 --> 00:00:13.701
the tenant and apps
provisioned from elsewhere.

6
00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:16.873
And there are app-specific
policies, one per app at most,

7
00:00:16.873 --> 00:00:19.975
which override the default
for whatever they define.

8
00:00:19.975 --> 00:00:23.649
Restrictions only bite on apps
created after a date you choose,

9
00:00:23.649 --> 00:00:26.900
and they never stop an existing
app from getting tokens.

10
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.225
They just refuse the
change that breaks them.

11
00:00:29.225 --> 00:00:33.700
Beta adds more restriction types, but
this chapter stays on version one.
